# Start App
npx expo start --clear
# When Running typ r in the terminal to refresh the app
# To push Changes to Expo hosting
eas update

# How to build Android to go to production
In app.Config version Has to go up by 1 
eas build -p android --profile production
Option B — manual upload:
Play Console → Testing → Internal testing → Create release → Upload the .aab.
Add testers (email list / Google Groups) → Save → Roll out.

# How to build IOs to go to Production
In app.Config version Has to go up by 1 
eas build --platform ios
eas submit --platform ios
eas submit --platform ios

# Firebase Analytics setup (iOS + Android)
1. In Firebase Console, open your project and add both apps:
   - iOS bundle ID: com.brody32.better
   - Android package: com.brody32.better
2. Download config files:
   - iOS: GoogleService-Info.plist -> place at project root as `GoogleService-Info.plist`
   - Android: google-services.json -> place at project root as `google-services.json`
3. Rebuild native apps (required after adding Firebase native dependencies):
   - Android: eas build -p android --profile production
   - iOS: eas build --platform ios
4. Screen tracking is now automatic from React Navigation.
   - Event name: `screen_view`
   - Params: `screen_name`, `screen_class`
5. In Firebase Console:
   - Go to Analytics -> Events (to verify events arrive)
   - Go to Analytics -> Engagement -> Pages and screens (to see most-used screens)

   npx eas-cli submit --platform android --id e0b29851-f31b-48a4-a067-d3df971ddcb8 --non-interactive 2>&1 | tail -25